{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance annual general adjustment cap (Measure BB)","requirement":"The Rent Board's annual general adjustment may not exceed 5% per year for fully covered units, though banked unused AGAs may still be applied. Government-owned or subsidized units become fully or partially covered and subject to a rent ceiling.","key_value":"AGA capped at 5% per year","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units include most units in multifamily properties built before 1980. New construction with a certificate of occupancy after 1980, most single-family homes and condominiums are only partially covered. Government-subsidized units are now fully or partially covered.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1980","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord who shares kitchen or bath facilities with the tenant and lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy","unit_limit":null},{"type":"other","text":"Government-owned or -subsidized units are now fully or partially covered; rent control depends on unit type and federal or state law."}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","New Construction Units (units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980)","Whether a unit is fully or partially covered depends on unit type and if Federal law, State law, or administrative regulation exempts the unit from the rent control provisions of Berkeley’s Rent Ordinance."]},"exemptions":"Units with a certificate of occupancy after 1980, most single-family homes and condominiums are only partially covered (no rent ceiling); units where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with a landlord who did not live on the property at the start of the tenancy are exempt.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Federal law, State law, or administrative regulation that prohibits rent control limits coverage of some subsidized units, making them only partially covered.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance just cause eviction changes (Measure BB)","requirement":"Landlords may evict tenants in fully or partially covered units only for just cause. Nonpayment eviction requires rental debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent, and eviction for refusing to sign a similar lease is barred.","key_value":"At least 1 month's Fair Market Rent rental debt required to evict for nonpayment","coverage_conditions":"Applies to tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance, including government-owned or -subsidized units. Units wholly exempt from the Ordinance, such as shared kitchen or bath units without a resident landlord, are not covered.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord who shares kitchen or bath facilities with the tenant and lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy","unit_limit":null},{"type":"other","text":"Government-owned or -subsidized units are now fully or partially covered; rent control depends on unit type and federal or state law."}],"per_tenancy":"Eviction allowed only for just cause; nonpayment requires rental debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent for a unit of equivalent size.","coverage_quotes":["In Berkeley, tenants in units that are fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance cannot be evicted unless there is \"just cause” (previously called “good cause”).","The landlord must file with the Rent Board a copy of any notice to terminate a tenancy, notice to quit, and summons and complaint no later than three business days after the tenant was served with the document.","Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
